# Prefer Naive UI
When building UI in Vue, use [Naive UI](https://www.naiveui.com/) components first. Do not create custom buttons, inputs, dialogs, tables, menus, or layout primitives if Naive already provides them.

## Rules
1. Prefer `naive-ui` for interactive and layout UI: `NButton`, `NInput`, `NSelect`, `NForm`, `NModal`, `NDrawer`, `NTabs`, `NDataTable`, `NSpace`, `NLayout`, `NMenu`, `NTag`, `NTooltip`, etc.
2. Import only what you use (tree-shake friendly), e.g. `import { NButton, NSpace } from 'naive-ui'`.
3. Use Naive props/slots/themes for styling and variants before writing custom CSS.
4. Custom components are OK only when wrapping Naive for app-specific reuse (e.g. `components/ui/AppConfirmModal.vue` around `NModal`) or when Naive has no equivalent.
5. Icons: prefer `@vicons/*` with Naive's `NIcon` when needed.

## Examples
```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD: custom button -->
<button class="btn-primary" @click="send">Send</button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { NButton } from 'naive-ui'
</script>
<template>
  <n-button type="primary" @click="send">Send</n-button>
</template>